\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{A historical event is not an update attempt}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{rollout}

\p{An immutable historical record prevents an update attempt from rewriting
the facts attached to its reused samples. The sample-reuse setup in
\citet{Section 3}{miao2026when} retains behavior-policy rollouts while
recomputing current-policy ratios. Dynamic Gradient Gating (DGG), defined in
\citet{Section 5 and Algorithm 1}{miao2026when}, is one such reuse protocol,
while the complete immutable tuple is a proposed interface for such protocols.}

\p{Recorded facts and estimates recomputed for an attempted update are
different objects; errors in the latter do not alter the former.}
